# Everything here would otherwise be uploaded to the daemon as build context and
# baked into the image. A lean context matters for three reasons: the upload is
# faster, the image is smaller, and -- most importantly -- a stray .env or
# courtvision.db must never end up inside a distributable image.

# Secrets. Never in an image.
.env

# Host-specific and rebuildable. .venv holds Linux-incompatible Windows
# binaries with absolute paths baked in; the image installs its own.
.venv/
venv/

# Generated state. The entrypoint runs seed.py, so a copied database would only
# be a stale one.
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Build artefacts and caches
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/

# History and tooling
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
replacements.txt

# Test output, which the compose volume maps in from the host instead
reports/
screenshots/

# Editor and OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Docs the running image has no use for. spikes/samples/*.json is NOT excluded:
# seed.py reads it, so the image genuinely needs it.
*.md
!README.md
